   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 152 of the laws of 2020 amending the environmental\nconservation law relating to authorizing hunting big game by rifle in the\ncounty of Tompkins, in relation to extending the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S9355",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9355-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 152 of 2020",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9355\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 152 of the laws of 2020 amending the environ-\nmental conservation law relating to authorizing hunting big game by\nrifle in the county of Tompkins, in relation to extending the effective-\nness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would extend an authorization allowing the hunting of big game\nthrough the use of a rifle in all of Tompkins County by two years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill would extend, until October 1, 2024, paragraph d\nof section 5 of Chapter 152 of the laws of 2020, which authorizes the\nhunting of big game by rifle in the county of Tompkins.\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that the bill shall take effect imme-\ndiately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTompkins County, by resolution, requested to be added to the list of\ncounties eligible to hunt big game with rifles. Since 2005, several\ncounties in the Finger Lakes Region, Central New York and the Southern\nTier have been permitted to hunt big game with rifles, with very few\nreported incidents or problems. This bill would extend the authorization\nfor Tompkins County to be included in that list for a limited, two-year\nperiod ending on October 1, 2024.\n\nThe continuation of a big game season and bag limits in Tompkins County\nis necessary to continue evaluating how the law is working in the coun-\nty. Additionally, failure to extend the authorization by October 1,\n2022, will disrupt wildlife management in Tompkins County.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
